first-run-printer-about {"x": -1920, "y": 4480, "w": 420, "page": "onboarding", "fill": "purple", "text": "Agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05 (“Go with your recommendations”). Kenneth signed up in the built app and landed on the add-printer dialog, “Step 1 of 3” with Cancel and Next, with nothing saying why; version 89 of 08 drew it that way. 08 now is a screen of its own: what the welcome finished, a headline that says why the app asks, brand, model and nozzle, Continue, and Skip for now with what skipping would do, shown only while no printer is chosen (agreed 2026-11-06). Once one is, its settings are read (18). No step counter, no Cancel, no plate or filament steps: the printer starts on its profile’s own plate and filament.

When AI is set up, “Can’t find your printer? Ask AI” under the menus opens Home with the printer chat.

OrcaSlicer on this computer shows 07 first, with the printers saved there and those ticked in its printer list (OrcaSlicer.conf “models”); Import shows what it brought (17), and Choose my printer instead shows 08. Imported names the filaments that came over, and one that couldn’t come over says to pick a similar one from the filament menu (agreed 2026-11-06)."} 

