content.text:
"See prices" now passes in the real app, but I'm stuck before the printer-setup screens. I started the combined `ui-walkthrough` build (473589d032) with a fresh profile and the staging server. Clicking "See prices" on the welcome card opened a "Credits and plans" sheet showing the staging prices page: the launch banner, the three offers ($10 credit pack, $10 Hobby, $20 Workshop) and "Sign up to buy" buttons. Closing it returned to the welcome screen. I sent you the screenshot.

Next I clicked "Just slice for now" to reach the printer-setup screens, but nothing happened, twice. The app's log shows the click never arrived. Your current desktop Space is a full-screen app, and macOS won't let me move the JusPrin window into it. Clicks into the window from behind it stopped getting through.

These are still untested in the real app:
- the JusPrin 1 import screen opening first when both JusPrin 1 and OrcaSlicer are found;
- the "Other ways" links between the three setup screens;
- a JusPrin 1 import going through to Home;
- File › Import from JusPrin 1….

The test app is still running, so I'll carry on from where it is. Can you switch your Mac to a regular desktop, not a full-screen app, and tell me when you have?

